+- `world.js` loads the real `index.html` and `js/app.js` into happy-dom before each scenario.
+
+## DOM-identity defect (active)
+
+R4 blockage: `render()` at js/app.js calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds all <li>
+from scratch. Real-browser acceptance suite fails with "element is no longer attached to the
+DOM" on every toggle interaction. In-harness suite passes because happy-dom re-queries the
+DOM between steps, hiding the detachment.
+
+Fix planted:
+- `features/dom-identity.feature` — 4 scenarios pinning the in-place-mutation contract
+- `watchbill.json` — single watch with dom-identity scenarios plus required existing scenarios
+- Perturbation at the seam in `render()` before `todoList.innerHTML = ''`
+
+The fix: assign `data-id` to each <li>; reconcile on render (mutate existing, create new,
+remove absent). Then remove the perturbation guard.
