@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+Feature: DOM element identity
+  As a user interacting through automated tools
+  I want todo DOM elements to stay attached when their completion state toggles
+  So that external assertions on the same element reference do not fail
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And there are no todos
+
+  Rule: Toggling a todo's completion must mutate the existing li element in place, not replace it
+
+  Scenario: Completing a single todo preserves its li element
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    When I capture the rendered todo list items
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for that todo
+    Then each captured item is still attached to the rendered list
+
+  Scenario: Un-completing a single todo preserves its li element
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    When I capture the rendered todo list items
+    And I un-complete "Buy milk"
+    Then each captured item is still attached to the rendered list
+
+  Rule: The toggle-all checkbox must mutate existing li elements in place
+
+  Scenario: Marking all as completed preserves all li elements
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Read book"
+    When I capture the rendered todo list items
+    And I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then each captured item is still attached to the rendered list
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the completed state preserves all li elements
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Read book"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    When I capture the rendered todo list items
+    And I click the toggle-all checkbox again
+    Then each captured item is still attached to the rendered list
